* "American 5153" power amp (service drawing 0070922000, supplied by the user): C64's coupling into the long-tailed ECC83 phase inverter V8 (R148 470 on the joined cathodes,
* R147 10k and R138 4.7k as the tail and the feedback node, R150 100k on the first grid, C63 .047u to the second), plates R133 82k / R184 100k with C71 47p across them,
* C52 / C47 (.047u) into four 6L6GC as two parallel pairs (1.5k grid stoppers, 220k grid returns to the bias supply, 100 ohm screen resistors, the cathodes through R186 (1 ohm:
* 80 mV across it is the bias setting), the output transformer with its 16 / 8 / 4 ohm sections (the impedance switch at 16 ohm) and the HT supply.
* The negative feedback and the presence / resonance network are not on the 5153 drawing: they are taken from the EVH 5150III service drawing (see below), which has the same phase inverter (R159 10k and R156 4.7k on the feedback node).

S VAUDIO pin 50k 0
S VHT a 1 485
S VBIAS bias 100 -63.5

C C64P pin ga 1u
R R150 ga j 100k
R R148 kk j 470
T V8A ga pa kk 12AX7
T V8B gb pb kk 12AX7
R R147 j n1 10k
R R138 n1 0 4.7k
C C63 gb n1 47n
R R151 j gb 100k
R R133 c pa 82k
R R184 c pb 100k
C C71 pa pb 47p

* Negative feedback, as in the EVH 5150III service drawing (PR4615A, sheet 2, the power amp breakaway PCB): from the 8 ohm tap (the ORG wire) through the
* RESONANCE rheostat R208 (1M audio taper) in parallel with C120 6n8 to the node nb, then R162 39k and C126 220u into the feedback node n1 (the junction of
* R159 10k and R156 4.7k). With the rheostat at 0 the feedback is flat; at 1M only the highs get through C120, so the feedback falls at low frequencies and the
* bass comes up.
R VR8 t8 nb 150k
C C120 t8 nb 6n8
R R162 nb nc 39k
C C126 nc n1 220u
* PRESENCE: R11 (10k rheostat, its wiper tied to the top end) in series with C3 + C11 (.068u each) from n1 to ground. At 0 ohm the caps shunt the highs of n1 to
* ground, the feedback falls at high frequencies and the highs come up; at 10k the shunt is mostly the resistor and the effect is small.
C C3_11 n1 pc 0.136u
R VRPR pc 0 5k

* Grid drive: C52 / C47 (.047u) from each plate, 220k returns to the bias supply (R111 / R110), 1.5k stoppers (R143 / R144 and R145 / R146).
C C52 pa d1 47n
C C47 pb d2 47n
R R111 d1 bias 220k
R R110 d2 bias 220k
C CBIAS bias 0 47u
R R143_4 d1 g910 1.5k/2
R R145_6 d2 g1112 1.5k/2

* 6L6GC pairs: V9 + V10 on one phase, V11 + V12 on the other; screens through 100 ohm (R134..R137) from B, cathodes through R186 (1 ohm).
P V9 g910 pt s910 kc 6L6GCDS 2
P V11 g1112 pbm s1112 kc 6L6GCDS 2
R R134_5 sb s910 100/2
R R136_7 sb s1112 100/2
R R186 kc 0 1

* Output transformer: plate-to-plate 2.6k, 3.5 H per primary half; windings are primary halves, then the 16, 8 and 4 ohm sections of the secondary.
R DCR_PT pt npt 40
R DCR_PBM pbm npb 40
.param n16 = 2*1/sqrt(2600/16)
.xfmr OT L=3.5 SAT=4.7
  W npt a 1 pri
  W a npb 1 pri
  W t16 t8 0.2929*n16 sec
  W t8 bk 0.2071*n16 sec
  W bk 0 0.5*n16 sec
  K pri pri 0.9998
  K pri sec 0.9993
  K sec sec 0.9998
.end
R RLOAD t16 0 16

* HT supply: reservoir A, the choke / filter, B (screens), the rail X for the preamp (R29 and C21X), C for V8's plates.
R T3 a sb 100
C C22 sb 0 100u
R R29 sb x 9.1k
C C21X x 0 47u
R RPREAMP x 0 25k
R R_C x c 2.2k
C C_C c 0 22u
